{:activity/_scope [{:activity/expected-seconds 960.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120672} :activity/id #uuid "6ede3e68-1ff6-5e3c-afed-499bb387f9a1" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048499} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120672 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186121034 :tutorial/content "Consider a vector $\\mathbf{u}$ which is given in terms of the vectors $\\mathbf{v_1}$ and $\\mathbf{v_2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}3}{\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v_1}}+({\\color{red}-2}){\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v_2}} = \\mathbf{u}\n$$\n\nHere, we say that $\\mathbf{u}$ is a **linear combination** of the vectors ${\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v_1}}$ and ${\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v_2}}$ with coefficients ${\\color{red}3}$ and ${\\color{red}-2}$ respectively. \n\nIn general, a linear combination of $n$ vectors $\\mathbf{v_1},\\mathbf{v_2},\\dots,\\mathbf{v_n}$ is the *weighted sum*\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}x_1}\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_1}+{\\color{red}x_2}\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_2}+\\cdots + {\\color{red}x_n}\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_n} = \\mathbf{u},\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\color{red}x_1},{\\color{red}x_2},\\dots,{\\color{red}x_n}\\in\\mathbb{R}.$ We say that $\\mathbf{u}$ is a linear combination of the vectors $\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_1},\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_2},\\dots,\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_n}$ with coefficients (or *weights*) ${\\color{red}x_1},{\\color{red}x_2},\\dots,{\\color{red}x_n},$ respectively.\n\nFor instance, \n![](images/ff/ff71636b9b5a34fec4de37b5e924c1c6bc3765c1ee823b325f5b0e01c0dc472a.svg)\nis the linear combination of vectors $\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_1},\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_2},\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_3}$ with coefficients ${\\color{red}2}, {\\color{red}0}, {\\color{red}\\dfrac{1}{2}},$ respectively." :tutorial/id #uuid "229ae855-226b-5f95-b050-b98257747800" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3186 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "b14c637b-1418-59f5-9ac3-37a07d6ad580" :step/math-academy-id 17456 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120673}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120673 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119805 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119616 :question/id #uuid "fd3cb5b1-f16e-5a52-82e4-25bbbd1c4fe7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4789" :question/problem "Find $s,$ if $3\\mathbf{a_1}+s\\mathbf{a_2} = \\mathbf{b}$ and\n![](images/c7/c715fd50dbcc9251cd7c01e033ba59be2af244d57ec02b707aa7cd8764e58d58.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $s$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+s{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 3\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}13 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}13 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}-3\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $s=4.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33586620-e110-5a37-874f-a92103c5e9fb" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048673} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049814}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542367 :question-generator/id #uuid "654ebed8-c886-576a-ae1a-ac9f64553608" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186119805.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120311 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71a2d12d-063a-5194-9872-f086deecbe0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315764} {:answer/id #uuid "b4f678bb-2e13-5906-beb2-95f91613edbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316142} {:answer/id #uuid "bb7b29bb-fb40-5f35-9053-65e121e4652d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218631